386	  /// `ChatRepository.retryMessage` when it's known, or falls back to a
387	  /// full [ChatRepository.sendMessage] resend of that same user content
388	  /// into this exact AI bubble slot when it's `null` (I/O matrix: "Tap
389	  /// retry, no `serverId`" — the stream dropped before `message_created`
390	  /// ever arrived, so the backend never actually persisted the question;
391	  /// Boundaries: "Never calling `chat-messages-retry` with no `serverId`").
392	  /// Reuses [_isSending] verbatim (Boundaries: "A second retry while one
393	  /// is in flight"), so this is a no-op while a send/retry is already in
394	  /// flight — and, like [sendMessage] (review finding), a no-op while
395	  /// [ChatReady.isOffline] too: a failed bubble's retry tap is a separate
396	  /// affordance from the composer, not covered by `_ChatComposer.canSend`
397	  /// alone, so it needs this exact same guard to honor the offline banner.
398	  Future<void> retryMessage(String aiMessageId) async {
